    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-129113",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-3,3].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-3,3].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =c \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-3,3]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14123896/assets/cdd8cec2d30ff2956d5210a49036c17d99781d0b62c0b0f42f97d0575c4d80f6.png)",
